WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.205
Let's make Meet the mud creatures.

2
00:00:02.585 --> 00:00:06.892
Shape a small, low mud creature and press in its expression with a smooth

3
00:00:06.892 --> 00:00:07.200
twig.

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:11.000
No tiny plastic eyes or permanent decoration needed.

5
00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:13.460
Make this project with a grown-up.

6
00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:16.570
Gather the supplies listed below the video.

7
00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.195
Pause whenever you need more time.

8
00:00:19.575 --> 00:00:23.230
An adult selects the soil and supervises contact.

9
00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:28.180
Avoid unknown or contaminated soil and keep mud away from mouths and eyes.

10
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:31.065
Use clean water and wash hands afterward.

11
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:33.690
Step 1.

12
00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:35.450
Mix a little mud.

13
00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:38.040
Put one cup of soil in the bowl.

14
00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:41.075
Add one tablespoon of water and stir.

15
00:00:41.455 --> 00:00:44.665
Repeat only until a squeezed handful holds together.

16
00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:48.685
Use less than the full quarter-cup if it already holds.

17
00:00:49.065 --> 00:00:50.445
Grown-up help.

18
00:00:50.825 --> 00:00:54.165
Choose the soil and help add water a little at a time.

19
00:00:55.667 --> 00:00:56.847
Step 2.

20
00:00:57.227 --> 00:00:58.632
Make a low body.

21
00:00:59.012 --> 00:01:01.592
Place a small handful on the tray.

22
00:01:01.972 --> 00:01:05.667
Press it into a mound no taller than about 5 centimetres.

23
00:01:06.047 --> 00:01:10.368
If it slumps, mix in a little dry soil; if it crumbles, add a

24
00:01:10.368 --> 00:01:11.602
few drops of water.

25
00:01:11.982 --> 00:01:13.362
Grown-up help.

26
00:01:13.742 --> 00:01:16.782
Help adjust the mixture if it will not hold.

27
00:01:18.167 --> 00:01:19.512
Step 3.

28
00:01:19.892 --> 00:01:21.797
Pinch ears or a tail.

29
00:01:22.177 --> 00:01:26.174
Use finger and thumb to pinch two ears from the same mound, or stretch

30
00:01:26.174 --> 00:01:27.887
one end into a short tail.

31
00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:31.852
Keep details thick and close to the body so they do not break off.

32
00:01:33.334 --> 00:01:34.484
Step 4.

33
00:01:34.864 --> 00:01:36.874
Press in a personality.

34
00:01:37.254 --> 00:01:41.195
Use the blunt end of the twig to make two shallow eye dents and

35
00:01:41.195 --> 00:01:42.039
a curved smile.

36
00:01:42.419 --> 00:01:45.974
Press short lines into the surface for fur or scales.

37
00:01:46.354 --> 00:01:48.634
Set the twig down between turns.

38
00:01:49.014 --> 00:01:50.394
Grown-up help.

39
00:01:50.774 --> 00:01:53.529
Help keep the tool away from faces.

40
00:01:55.001 --> 00:01:56.176
Step 5.

41
00:01:56.556 --> 00:01:58.391
Introduce your new friend.

42
00:01:58.771 --> 00:02:00.906
Leave the creature on its tray.

43
00:02:01.286 --> 00:02:03.671
Give it a name and tell one thing it likes.

44
00:02:04.051 --> 00:02:08.606
Gather tools and wash hands with soap and running water before another activity.

45
00:02:08.986 --> 00:02:10.366
Grown-up help.

46
00:02:10.746 --> 00:02:13.686
Help with handwashing and contain muddy cleanup.

47
00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:18.083
Here are three ideas for your finished project.

48
00:02:18.463 --> 00:02:22.013
These example pictures were made with artificial intelligence.

49
00:02:22.393 --> 00:02:24.413
Your creation can look different.

50
00:02:24.793 --> 00:02:26.773
Keep soil out of indoor drains.

51
00:02:27.153 --> 00:02:31.368
Separate tools and dispose of or return suitable soil only where permitted.

52
00:02:31.748 --> 00:02:34.463
Mud is temporary and may crack as it dries.

53
00:02:34.843 --> 00:02:37.808
A photograph or drawing can preserve its character.

54
00:02:38.188 --> 00:02:39.178
Well done.

55
00:02:39.558 --> 00:02:41.988
Take a moment to enjoy what you made.

